   205	    The GEMM-backend setting's name, its source gating of the Triton templates
   206	    and the overflow it avoids are version-specific, so an unprobed stack fails
   207	    before anything compiles. A host without CUDA cannot run Triton kernels or
   208	    report a driver; those two checks are skipped with an explicit reason and
   209	    happen on GPU hosts.
